			(name "DESCRIPTION") "The BMS master board is the bridge between the TIM and the 16 BMS slave boards. It passes data both ways over a looped daisy chain, isolated by transformers so the battery’s high voltage never reaches the low-voltage side, and it signals the TIM the moment any slave reports a fault.")
